# Scope: course tracker (only this)

The app **only records progress** through Vladislav's courses:
- Courses → modules → pieces (e.g. `CUR-1` → `CUR-1.1`), each piece has a **done** mark.
- Progress per module and per course (counts / %). That's all.
- Data source: `/workspace/learning-system/courses-v2/` (`cursor.md`, `discrete.md`, `claude.md`). Parse headings `## <ID> · <title>` (module) and `### <ID> · <title>` (piece); a `✅` in a piece heading = initially done. Copy/bundle the data into the repo at build time; the app never fetches it at runtime.
- Offline PWA, works on phone and iPad. Done marks persist locally (IndexedDB/localStorage, versioned). No accounts, no backend, no network calls.

## Out of scope — do not build
No queue/planner, no "what's next", no learning techniques (SRS, Anki, Feynman, interleaving, mind maps, voice), no AI/LLM calls or API keys, no stats beyond progress, no notifications, no gamification. Old module code in `src/modules/*` and `src/agent/` is legacy: don't extend it; remove it only when the user asks.

## Design (APPROVED by Vladislav, 2026-10-12) — follow exactly
- Minimalist but alive. Dark background, large type, big touch targets (iPad + phone).
- Home: horizontal snap-scrolling carousel of course cards + a "+ Курс" card. Each card: course's large minimalist image, title, progress bar with "12 / 45". Color + image come from course .md frontmatter (`color`, `image`).
- Course screen: modules expand into pieces (title + short goal) with a round check. Checking flashes the course color; bar grows smoothly. Finishing a module → small confetti. Done pieces greyed out.
- Smooth screen transitions: View Transitions API with CSS fallback; respect prefers-reduced-motion.
- Add course: import .md (courses-v2 format incl. frontmatter; image = URL, data:/inline SVG, or bundled path) or create manually (title, modules, steps).
- Progress in localStorage; JSON export/import. Legacy src/modules, src/agent may be removed for this tracker.
- Nothing else.

## Behaviour
- Don't invent features, screens, settings or copy. If something is unclear, stop and ask.
- Small steps; one change per run. Don't push or deploy unless asked.
